{"_v":1,"id":"spring-awakening-2006","bd":{"positive":3,"mixed":0,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2006/legit/reviews/spring-awakening-1200516066/","d":"2006-12-11","q":"This strange, beguiling show is by no means flawless, but with subtle, nurturing changes, the creative team and cast have fashioned an already seductive work into something even more lovely and lyrical."},{"cn":"Peter Marks","o":"The Washington Post","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/archive/lifestyle/2006/12/11/spring-awakening-blooms-on-broadway/","d":"2006-12-11","q":"Spring Awakening is a musical of exceptional power and beauty, a show that succeeds in making the late 19th century feel urgently contemporary."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":81,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2006/12/11/theater/reviews/11spri.html","d":"2006-12-11","q":"A straight shot of eroticism steamed open last night at the Eugene O’Neill Theater under the innocuous name of “Spring Awakening,” and Broadway, with its often puerile sophistication and its sterile romanticism, may never be the same."}],"au":{"score":91,"designation":"Loving","sources":{"mz":{"s":90,"c":224,"sr":4.5},"ss":{"s":92,"c":550}}},"hi":"/images/shows/spring-awakening-2006/hero.webp","ta":"230 W 49th St, New York, NY 10019","pd":"2006-11-16","ca":[{"n":"Skylar Astin","r":"Georg"},{"n":"Gerard Canonico","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Lilli Cooper","r":"Martha"},{"n":"Jennifer Damiano","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Christine Estabrook","r":"The Adult Women"},{"n":"John Gallagher Jr.","r":"Moritz"},{"n":"Gideon Glick","r":"Ernst"},{"n":"Jonathan Groff","r":"Melchior"},{"n":"Robert Hager","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Brian Charles Johnson","r":"Otto"},{"n":"Lea Michele","r":"Wendla"},{"n":"Lauren Pritchard","r":"Ilse"},{"n":"Krysta Rodriguez","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Stephen Spinella","r":"The Adult Men"},{"n":"Phoebe Strole","r":"Anna"},{"n":"Jona